{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_2_operators_15_comma_void_in_delete_delete_holes", "label": "delete creates array holes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-2-operators/15-comma-void-in-delete.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "delete arr[1] leaves length 3 and 1 in arr false. map preserves holes. Use splice/filter/toSpliced. Returns true even if the key never existed."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_2_operators_15_comma_void_in_delete_in_vs_hasown", "label": "in vs Object.hasOwn", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-2-operators/15-comma-void-in-delete.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'toString' in {} is true (prototype). hasOwn is false. hasOwn distinguishes missing from present-undefined. On arrays in tests indices."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_2_operators_15_comma_void_in_delete_void", "label": "void operator", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-2-operators/15-comma-void-in-delete.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Evaluates operand, always returns undefined. void 0 was a safe undefined before ES5. Modern leftover: discard a floating promise for a linter."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_2_operators_15_comma_void_in_delete_comma", "label": "Comma operator", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-2-operators/15-comma-void-in-delete.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Evaluates left to right, returns last. Lowest precedence so x=1,2,3 assigns 1. One readable use: two-pointer for header."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_2_operators_05_loops_